---
import CalculatorLayout from '../../../layouts/CalculatorLayout.astro';
import Formula from '../../../components/Formula.astro';

const f = {
  fwd: "$$\\text{tsp} = \\text{ml} \\div 4.92892$$",
  rev: "$$\\text{ml} = \\text{tsp} \\times 4.92892$$",
};

const tocItems = [
  { id: 'how-to-use',      label: 'How to use this converter' },
  { id: 'formula',         label: 'How to convert ml to teaspoons' },
  { id: 'reference-table', label: 'ml to teaspoons reference table' },
  { id: 'faq',             label: 'FAQs' },
  { id: 'related-tools',   label: 'Related tools' },
];

const schema = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "WebApplication",
    "name": "Milliliters to Teaspoons Converter",
    "url": "https://calculations.tools/conversion/volume-converter/ml-to-tsp",
    "description": "Convert milliliters to teaspoons for cooking and medicine. 5 ml = 1 tsp, 10 ml = 2 tsp, 15 ml = 1 tablespoon = 3 tsp.",
    "applicationCategory": "UtilitiesApplication",
    "operatingSystem": "Any",
    "browserRequirements": "Requires JavaScript",
    "isAccessibleForFree": true,
    "offers": { "@type": "Offer", "price": "0", "priceCurrency": "USD" }
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "HowTo",
    "name": "How to convert milliliters to teaspoons",
    "description": "Divide ml by 4.92892 to get teaspoons.",
    "step": [
      { "@type": "HowToStep", "position": 1, "name": "Enter ml value", "text": "Type your ml value in the ml field. The teaspoon result updates instantly." },
      { "@type": "HowToStep", "position": 2, "name": "Read the result", "text": "The converted teaspoon value appears. For 5 ml, the result is 1.01 teaspoons." },
      { "@type": "HowToStep", "position": 3, "name": "Convert in reverse", "text": "Type in the teaspoons field to convert back to ml." }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    "mainEntity": [
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "How many teaspoons is 5 ml?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "5 ml equals 1.014 teaspoons - essentially 1 teaspoon. Medical dosing standardizes 1 teaspoon to exactly 5 ml." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "How many teaspoons is 10 ml?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "10 ml equals 2.029 teaspoons - about 2 teaspoons. Many liquid medicines specify 10 ml as a dose, described as 2 teaspoons." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "How many teaspoons is 15 ml?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "15 ml equals 3.04 teaspoons - about 3 teaspoons or 1 tablespoon. The exact tablespoon is 14.787 ml." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "How many teaspoons is 2.5 ml?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "2.5 ml equals 0.507 teaspoons - about half a teaspoon. This is a common children's medicine dose." } }
    ]
  }
];
---
<CalculatorLayout
  title="Milliliters to Teaspoons Converter"
  metaTitle="Milliliters to Teaspoons Converter | Convert ml to tsp"
  description="Convert ml to teaspoons for cooking and medicine. 5 ml = 1 tsp, 10 ml = 2 tsp, 2.5 ml = 1/2 tsp. Enter ml or teaspoons - converts both directions."
  canonical="https://calculations.tools/conversion/volume-converter/ml-to-tsp"
  tocItems={tocItems}
  embedSlug="ml-to-tsp"
  schema={schema}
  ogFormula="tsp = ml ÷ 4.92892"
  ogExample="5 ml = 1 teaspoon"
>
  <div slot="calculator">
    <section class="calculator-interface">
      <div class="calculator-container">
        <div class="calculator-header">
          <h2>Instantly Convert ml to tsp</h2>
          <p>Type in either field - converts instantly in both directions</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pair-inputs">
          <div class="pair-field">
            <label for="lp-a">Milliliters (ml)</label>
            <input id="lp-a" type="text" inputmode="decimal" placeholder="e.g. 5" />
          </div>
          <div class="pair-eq">=</div>
          <div class="pair-field">
            <label for="lp-b">Teaspoons (tsp)</label>
            <input id="lp-b" type="text" inputmode="decimal" placeholder="e.g. 1" />
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="pair-formula-note">1 tsp = 4.92892 ml &nbsp;·&nbsp; 5 ml ≈ 1 tsp (medical)</div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <script src="/js/ml-to-tsp.js" is:inline></script>
  </div>
  <div slot="content">
    <div class="seo-container">
      <div class="answer-box">
        <div class="answer-box-label">Quick answer</div>
        <p>To convert milliliters to teaspoons, divide by <strong>4.92892</strong>. So 5 ml = 1 teaspoon, 10 ml = 2 teaspoons, and 15 ml = 3 teaspoons (1 tablespoon). In medicine, 5 ml is officially defined as 1 teaspoon for dosing.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="answer-box">
        <div class="answer-box-label">Key takeaways</div>
        <ul>
          <li>Formula: tsp = ml ÷ 4.92892. Medical standard: 5 ml = 1 teaspoon exactly.</li>
          <li>2.5 ml = 1/2 tsp. 5 ml = 1 tsp. 10 ml = 2 tsp. 15 ml = 3 tsp = 1 tbsp.</li>
          <li>Quick check: for medicine doses, dividing by 5 ml gives approximate teaspoons.</li>
          <li>Reverse: ml = tsp × 4.92892.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <h2 id="how-to-use">How to use our ml to tsp converter</h2>
      <p>Type any ml value in the ml field and the teaspoon result appears instantly. For medicine doses, dividing by 5 is a quick mental check. Both directions work without pressing a button.</p>
      <h2 id="formula">How do you convert ml to teaspoons?</h2>
      <p>Divide the number of milliliters by 4.92892. For medicine, the FDA defines 1 teaspoon as exactly 5 ml for over-the-counter dosing, making 5 ml the practical standard. The exact US culinary teaspoon (4.929 ml) differs by less than 2%.</p>
      <Formula expr={f.fwd} />
      <p>Worked examples: 1 ml = 0.203 tsp. 2.5 ml = 0.507 tsp (1/2 tsp). 5 ml = 1.01 tsp (1 tsp). 10 ml = 2.03 tsp (2 tsp). 15 ml = 3.04 tsp (1 tbsp). 30 ml = 6.09 tsp (2 tbsp). 60 ml = 12.17 tsp (4 tbsp).</p>
      <h2 id="reference-table">Milliliters to teaspoons reference table</h2>
      <p>Common ml amounts expressed as teaspoons - for both cooking and medicine:</p>
      <div class="responsive-table">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Milliliters (ml)</th><th>Teaspoons (tsp)</th><th>Context</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>1.25 ml</td><td>0.25 tsp (1/4)</td><td>Spice pinch / tiny dose</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2.5 ml</td><td>0.51 tsp (1/2)</td><td>Children's dose (half tsp)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>5 ml</td><td>1.01 tsp (1)</td><td>Standard medicine dose</td></tr>
            <tr><td>7.5 ml</td><td>1.52 tsp (1.5)</td><td>-</td></tr>
            <tr><td>10 ml</td><td>2.03 tsp (2)</td><td>Common medicine dose</td></tr>
            <tr><td>12.5 ml</td><td>2.54 tsp (2.5)</td><td>-</td></tr>
            <tr><td>15 ml</td><td>3.04 tsp (3)</td><td>1 tablespoon</td></tr>
            <tr><td>20 ml</td><td>4.06 tsp</td><td>-</td></tr>
            <tr><td>30 ml</td><td>6.09 tsp</td><td>2 tablespoons / 1 fl oz</td></tr>
            <tr><td>60 ml</td><td>12.17 tsp</td><td>4 tablespoons / 1/4 cup</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <h2 id="faq">FAQs about converting ml to tsp</h2>
      <h3>How many teaspoons is 5 ml?</h3>
      <p>5 ml equals just over 1 teaspoon (1.014 tsp exactly). For medicine, 5 ml is defined as exactly 1 teaspoon by the FDA. For cooking, 5 ml vs 4.93 ml makes no practical difference.</p>
      <h3>How many teaspoons is 10 ml?</h3>
      <p>10 ml equals 2.03 teaspoons - essentially 2 teaspoons. Liquid medicine doses of 10 ml are described as 2 teaspoons on US labels.</p>
      <h3>How many teaspoons is 15 ml?</h3>
      <p>15 ml equals 3.04 teaspoons - about 3 teaspoons or 1 tablespoon. 15 ml is the common rounding for 1 tablespoon (actual: 14.787 ml).</p>
      <h3>How many teaspoons is 2.5 ml?</h3>
      <p>2.5 ml equals 0.507 teaspoons - half a teaspoon. This is a common children's medicine dose, specified as "1/2 teaspoon" on many labels.</p>
      <h2 id="related-tools">Related tools</h2>
      <ul class="related-tools-list">
        <li>
          <span class="tool-icon">💧</span>
          <div>
            <a href="/conversion/volume-converter/tsp-to-ml">Teaspoons to Milliliters</a>
            <p>Reverse conversion - enter teaspoons and get ml instantly.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="tool-icon">💧</span>
          <div>
            <a href="/conversion/volume-converter/ml-to-tbsp">Milliliters to Tablespoons</a>
            <p>Convert ml to tablespoons - 15 ml = 1 tablespoon.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="tool-icon">💧</span>
          <div>
            <a href="/conversion/volume-converter/ml-to-fl-oz">Milliliters to Fluid Ounces</a>
            <p>Convert ml to fl oz - 30 ml = 1 fl oz = 6 teaspoons.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="tool-icon">💧</span>
          <div>
            <a href="/conversion/volume-converter">Volume Converter (all units)</a>
            <p>Convert between all volume units - ml, L, fl oz, cups, gallons, and more.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</CalculatorLayout>
<style is:global>
  .pair-inputs { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr; gap: 0.75rem; align-items: end; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .pair-field label { display: block; font-size: 0.8rem; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.7); margin-bottom: 0.35rem; }
  .pair-field input { width: 100%; padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.08); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.15); border-radius: 8px; color: white; font-size: 1rem; box-sizing: border-box; }
  .pair-eq { font-size: 1.5rem; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.5); padding-bottom: 0.35rem; }
  .pair-formula-note { text-align: center; font-size: 0.75rem; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.45); margin-top: 0.5rem; }
  @media (max-width: 480px) { .pair-inputs { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .pair-eq { text-align: center; padding-bottom: 0; } }
</style>